From e09da3439a3ceb94b0313414872eb53e14bbaf82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:30:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): one busy board degrades only itself in sidebar
 activity reads [daveey]

kanban-359833be53: while another thread held a board's lifecycle lock, board_memo_key()
re-opened the board the cheap content probe had just found busy (the probe falls back to
the stat exactly then), raised "database is locked: board lifecycle is busy" with no SQLite
error code, and annotate_kanban_activity marked EVERY chat row kanban_unknown.
session_tasks failed the same way (66 hits in always-on-dashboard.log).

- kanban_generation: lifecycle_access raises BoardLifecycleBusy (OperationalError,
  sqlite_errorcode=SQLITE_BUSY); shared is_busy() predicate (retry_open uses it).
- revalidate.board_memo_key: busy -> (stat key, BusyToken(error)), never matching a memo row.
- new kanban_session_activity_busy: a busy board with a usable memo row reuses its last
  good counts (never a second busy budget after a busy memo key), keeps that memo row, logs
  one WARNING "kanban board %s busy; reused last counts" (no traceback) and marks the
  published counts non-revalidatable; session_tasks on a busy board serves its last good
  list for the same query with every row stale=True (bounded memo, 512 entries).
- A busy board never read before still raises: unknown, never "no work".

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_busy_board_activity.py (4 red before, 5 green after).
